## Where the PHY work stands

All code is written and in the working tree; nothing is committed.

**Migration numbering — please note.** The coordinator asked for `006.do.sql`/`006.undo.sql`, but **006 was already taken**: another session added it while I was working (it converts the unreported address type from `1` to a `-1` sentinel), and it is already applied to the live capture at schemaversion 6. Editing it would break postgrator's checksum on the running install — the same constraint as before. My work is therefore **`007.do.sql` / `007.undo.sql`**.

**Schema decision.** Last value plus three sticky flags:

| column | why |
|---|---|
| `last_phy` | nullable — `NULL` is the third state, not 1M |
| `last_extended` | 1 extended, 0 legacy, `NULL` never reported |
| `ever_coded`, `ever_extended` | sticky — say *why* a device is unreachable |
| `ever_legacy_1m` | sticky — **the actual answer** |

I deviated from the suggested pair, deliberately. "Ever heard on Coded" does not answer "would a legacy-only scan lose this device" — a device heard on Coded *and* on legacy 1M loses nothing. A legacy scanner receives legacy advertisements on 1M and nothing else, so the answer is `ever_legacy_1m`; the other two are kept to label *why*. Sticky rather than last-value because a device can be heard both ways and the last sweep flaps.

The three flags are `NOT NULL DEFAULT 0`, so `0` is indistinguishable from "never observed at all" — and those are opposite answers. `formatDevice` gates them on `last_phy !== null` and exposes `legacyReachable: boolean | null`, mirroring the `manufacturer` pattern. It also **drops** `ever_legacy_1m` from the response rather than spreading it, so no caller can read the ungated number (a leak I caught when a test diff showed it).

Parser rejects `phy` outside {1, 3} — 2M is a secondary PHY only — and drops `ext` with it, since without a `phy` an absent `ext` is silence, not "legacy". Page keeps it quiet: grey `1M`, grey dash for "firmware cannot tell", and a warning tag only on `Coded only` / `ext only`.

